    "body": "When a fetch completes you would get a task (and within that a microtask).\r\n\r\nIt sounds like we want to do this at the end of \"perform a microtask checkpoint\" since that happens at the end-of-task or after each listener (when the event is synthetic). (Basically whenever the JavaScript execution context stack is empty.) @domenic knows this better than I do though.",
