    "created_at": "2017-01-30T18:21:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-01-30T18:21:33Z",
    "body": "I believe just the current task is adequate. (I see most hooks associated with a loop rather than a task, e.g. the \"perform a microtask checkpoint\" steps have an event loop as context, not a task, which is why I was fixated on the event loop)\r\n\r\nThis should not span multiple tasks to my knowledge. If there are any special cases where multiple tasks have special behavior (e.g. are executed within one \"turn\" of the event loop, other than microtasks) then we should test and see how implementations behave.",
